         detail_en="Two agents, A and B, isolated from each other on the network, still share one host and therefore one set-associative CPU cache. A direct network message between them (/agents/relay) is always refused. A can still hand its secret to B with Prime+Probe: B primes every cache set, A evicts a set to signal a bit, and B probes to read it back. The timing is modelled deterministically; the eviction mechanism is real and scripts/cache_covert_probe.py attempts the real wall-clock version. While on, the two agents share one cache medium and B reconstructs A's secret bit by bit; while off, the cache is partitioned per agent so A cannot signal B, yet an agent still uses its own cache (sender equal to receiver keeps working).",
